 fixSendEvents(id props);event;m;names;values;one;i;vcf;ns;vals;fs;ct
⍝ props is an object about to be sent to the client
⍝ do not send numeric events or Close

 props.⎕EX'Data' 'ChildList' 'EventList' 'PropList' ⍝ Never send these to JS client

 :If 0≠≢names←'Options' 'Series'~⍨props.⎕NL-9              ⍝ Do not try to serialise namespaces
     values←,props⍎⍕names
     values←(1+≢⍕caller)↓¨⍕¨values
     ⍎'props.(',(⍕names),')←',(1≠≢names)↓'⊃values'
 :EndIf

 :If 0≠≢names←props.⎕NL-2
     values←,⊂⍣(one←1=≢names)⊢props⍎⍕names
 :AndIf 0≠≢i←⍸(2=≡¨values)∧0=≢∘⍴¨values ⍝ Cannot JSONify enclosed scalars
     values[i]←⊃¨values[i]
     ⍎'props.(',(⍕names[i]),')←',(1≠≢i)↓'⊃values[i]'
 :EndIf

 :If ∨/m←0≠props.⎕NC vcf←'Values' 'CellTypes' 'FormatString'
 :AndIf (⊂caller⍎id,'.Type')∊,⊂'Grid'
     vals←(caller⍎id)⍎⍕vcf
     (m/vals)←props⍎(1≠+/m)↓'⊂',⍕m/vcf
     (vals ct fs)←vals
     :If ~0∊∊⍴¨fs ct
         ⍝ CellTypes need not conform to Values. Native never reshapes it on a
         ⍝ Values write (measured - see tests/test_gridShadowProps) and looks it
         ⍝ up lazily per painted cell, so a stale CellTypes is legal there and
         ⍝ simply never indexed out of range. We format the whole matrix in one
         ⍝ go, so emulate that lazy lookup - trim/pad to ⍴vals and clamp into
         ⍝ fs's index range - rather than LENGTH ERRORing on the mismatch.
         :If ((⍴ct)≢⍴vals)∨∨/,(ct<⎕IO)∨ct>¯1+⎕IO+≢fs
             ⍝ Warning, not Debug: native tolerates this silently, but in EWC a
             ⍝ persistent mismatch is usually the app miscomputing a row/column
             ⍝ count, and a silent conform would hide that.
             'W'Log'Grid ',id,': CellTypes ',(⍕⍴ct),' vs Values ',(⍕⍴vals),' - conforming'
             ct←(¯1+⎕IO+≢fs)⌊⎕IO⌈(⍴vals)↑ct ⍝ ↑ pads with 0: INDEX ERROR under ⎕IO←1
         :EndIf
⍝         props.FormattedValues←,¨fs[ct]⎕FMT¨⍉∘⍪¨vals
         props.FormattedValues←fs[ct]format1Cell¨vals
     :EndIf
 :EndIf

 :If 0≠props.⎕NC'Event'
     event←⊃¨props.Event
     event←(2×(2↑¨event)∊⊂'on')↓¨event
     :If ∨/m←~((10|⎕DR¨event)∊1 3)∨event∊⊂'Close'
         props.Event←m/props.Event
         (2⊃¨props.Event)←⊂''               ⍝ Blank out extra info /// will soon send only the Event name
     :Else
         props.⎕EX'Event'
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
